<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sanur is a coastal district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denpasar">Denpasar</a> on the south-east coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. It is the site of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belanjong-pillar">Belanjong pillar</a> of 914, the oldest dated inscription on the island. In the 20th century it became one of Bali's first beach resorts and a home to foreign artists.</p></div>
